OL,3,GNEWSA'A huge vanity project' - when
OL,4,ASputnik crash-landed in Scotland
OL,5,
OL,6,FTen years ago, an alien object entered
OL,7,FScotland's airspace for the first time.
OL,9,FThe website and internet radio station
OL,10,FSputnik News was named after the first
OL,11,Fman-made satellite which was launched
OL,12,Finto space in 1957.
OL,14,FThe size of a basketball, the original
OL,15,FSputnik emitted a simple beep for three
OL,16,Fweeks before its battery died.
OL,18,FBut the signal it sent the world's
OL,19,Fgovernments was much more significant.
OL,20,FIt showed that the Soviet Union was
OL,21,Fwinning the space race, and that news
OL,22,Fjolted the west into action.
OL,23,APub: 28-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
